cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Focal Prompt
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jenkins
    given-names: Thomas
repository-code: https://github.com/thomjenkins/focalprompt
url: https://focalprompt.com
abstract: >-
  Focal Prompt is an open-source research toolkit for studying how language
  models allocate attention and respond to their informational environment.
  It compares reported focus (model self-assessment of a completion) with
  perturbation-derived behavioural sensitivity (leave-one-focus-out ablation,
  embedding distance, permutation testing, and Benjamini–Hochberg FDR control).
keywords:
  - large language models
  - behavioural ecology
  - prompt ablation
  - permutation test
  - interpretability
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-20"
